        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Curtain of yellow silk satin damask. Repeat of 46.75 inches with large blooms filling the width of the fabric, and with smaller flowers, fruits, leaves and corn on a fleshy stem. The design is in satin with the background in 1/2 twill. The selvedges are narrow and are woven with multicoloured silks."@en , "Curtain of silk satin damask, possibly made in France, 1835-1850."@en ;
